cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, the derived data or the results, please cite it as below. Please also cite the original datasets (Belebele, Global-MMLU), listed in the paper."
title: "Language and Script Gaps in Local Language Models for Indian Users"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-23
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Dorkar
    given-names: Om
abstract: >-
  An offline audit of five open-weight language models (Gemma 3 12B, Qwen3 8B, Llama 3.1 8B,
  gpt-oss 20B, Sarvam-30B) running fully offline on one laptop. It compares accuracy on the same
  Belebele and Global-MMLU questions in English, 13 Indian languages, native versus romanized script,
  synthetic Indian English and synthetic Hinglish, and tests two preprocessing fixes
  (transliteration to native script, translation to English). Code, item samples, machine-made
  conditions and model outputs (76,400 answers) are released. Code is MIT; derived data is CC BY-SA 4.0.
keywords:
  - Indian languages
  - multilingual evaluation
  - romanization
  - code-mixing
  - fairness audit
  - on-device language models
  - benchmark evaluation
repository-code: "https://github.com/omdorkar/local-language-models-india"
